# Cron alternative to the systemd timer. Rebuilds daily and reloads the server.
# Install: `crontab -e` (as the cloudattr user) and add the line below.
#
# The build is atomic and fail-closed: a failed fetch/parse leaves the previous
# cloud.mmdb untouched, so a bad run never takes the server down. `pkill -HUP`
# tells a running `cloudattr serve` to hot-swap the new file.
#
# Rebuild every day at 03:17 (offset from the hour to avoid mirror thundering herd):
17 3 * * *  cd /var/lib/cloudattr && /usr/local/bin/cloudattr build --out cloud.mmdb --csv cloud.csv >> /var/log/cloudattr/build.log 2>&1 && pkill -HUP -f 'cloudattr serve'

# To build from an internal mirror, prefix with the env override:
# 17 3 * * *  CLOUDIP_REZMOSS_BASE=https://mirror.internal/cloudip/ /usr/local/bin/cloudattr build --out /var/lib/cloudattr/cloud.mmdb ...
